{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Sally in Spain"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "A Travel Journal"}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "scholar > Celebrating Important Occasions > Running of the Bulls"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 5}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use information about travel and vacations in social situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Placeholder"}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Placeholder"}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": ""}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": ""}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": ""}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": ""}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": ""}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": ""}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Writing A Travel Journal"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You write a travel journal to document and remember new places, cultures and experiences.<br/><br/>A travel journal is similar to a diary.  They are usually small enough to carry in your hand luggage while you travel.<br/>You usually use the Simple Past tense when you write in a travel journal because you usually write about things after they happen.<br/>A travel diary entry often includes:<br/><br/><li>A location and date in the title<br/><li>Who you traveled with<br/><li>Where you stayed and if you enjoyed it<br/><li>Who you met and their contact information<br/><li>Places to eat and your comments<br/><li>Things to see and if you would visit again<br/><br/>Sometimes, a travel journal entry can be about an experience like watching the \u201cRunning of the Bulls\u201d or another event.<br/><br/>Your travel diary should have enough detail for you to visit an area again."}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use in a travel journal."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le05ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "barrier  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " something that prevents or blocks movement from one place to another "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There were barriers along the sides of the street."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le05ob08aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to chase"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the act of following and trying to catch "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The bulls were chasing the men."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le05ob08aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "suddenly "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very quickly in an unexpected way "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Suddenly, hundreds of people started filling the streets."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le05ob08aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to explore  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to go through a place to learn more about it  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I decided to explore the city."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le05ob08aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "herd  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a large group of the same animal"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A herd of bulls chased the men down the street. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le05ob08aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to trample  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to tread on or crush "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The bulls trampled the man."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le05ob08aud06"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Interview a friend or family member about a holiday or vacation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ask these questions: <ul><li>What was the location and date of yourtrip?</li> <li>Who did you traveled with ?</li> <li>Where did you stay? Did you enjoy it?</li> <li>Who did you meet? Did you get theircontact information?</li> <li>Where did you eat? Was it good?</li> <li>What would you see again if you returned?</li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " Use this information to write their travel diary."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I interview a friend or family member about a vacation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I ask questions about their holiday."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a travel journal for another person."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write complete statements about travel."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn4le05ob08re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn4le05ob08re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn4le05ob08re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Travel Journal July 7th Pamplona, Spain</span>", "id": 1, "time": "50", "image": "engenn4le05ob08re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "I arrived in Pamplona late last night, and today I decided to explore. I was walking around the city, enjoying the sights, when suddenly hundreds of people started filling the streets.", "id": 2, "time": "4000", "image": "engenn4le05ob08re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "They were very excited and they were all moving in the same direction. I wanted to know where they were going, so I followed them.", "id": 3, "time": "17000", "image": "engenn4le05ob08re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "Soon we came to a very wide street with barriers along the side. People stood behind the barriers. Suddenly, everyone stopped talking and looked towards one end of the street. A group of men were running down the street as fast as they could, with a herd of bulls chasing them! Someone was trampled. It was all over very fast, but it was definitely an incredible experience! The town festival was the highlight of my vacation so far.", "id": 4, "time": "25000", "image": "engenn4le05ob08re2img03.jpg"}, {"text": "The hotel I am staying at ...", "id": 5, "time": "54000", "image": "engenn4le05ob08re2img03.jpg"}]}}]}, {"id": 2, "type": "video", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "video", "value": {"video_src": "engenn4le05ob08re3vid01", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": ""}, {"text": "<span class = \"bullet\">A travel journal</span>", "id": 1, "time": "5000", "image": ""}, {"text": "<span class = \"bullet\"> What do you include?</span>", "id": 2, "time": "12000", "image": ""}]}}]}], "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Listening"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Vocabulary and Grammar"}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can write about what I did."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can express opinions about other people and things in a written way."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can write a short travel journal."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Are you a thrill seeker? Why or why not?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Do you like to do things that are dangerous like skydiving or do you prefe